---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import chart from '../assets/ozan/ozan_slop_chart.png';
import banner from '../assets/ozan/ozan_banner.png';

const jsonLdApp = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
  name: 'Ozan-v1-12B',
  applicationCategory: 'DeveloperApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'Any',
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Arbaz Siddiqui' },
  url: 'https://www.arbazsiddiqui.me/ozan',
  offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
};
const jsonLd = [jsonLdApp, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://www.arbazsiddiqui.me/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Projects", "item": "https://www.arbazsiddiqui.me/projects/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Ozan-12B", "item": "https://www.arbazsiddiqui.me/ozan/"}]}];
---

<Base
  title="Ozan-v1-12B: Creative-Writing LLM"
  description="A 12B Mistral-Nemo fine-tune for natural-sounding fiction, with the lowest 12B slop score on EQ-Bench Creative Writing v3 and 3K+ downloads."
  ogImage="/og/ozan.jpg"
  ogImageAlt="Ozan-v1-12B, an open 12B language model tuned for fiction writing."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="narrow section">
    <p class="kicker">Open-weights LLM · June 2026</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Ozan-v1-12B</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A language model tuned to write long-form fiction that doesn't read
      like a machine wrote it. <em>Ozan</em> is Turkish for storyteller.
    </p>

    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>Base</dt><dd>Mistral-Nemo-Instruct-2407 (12B)</dd>
      <dt>Method</dt><dd>QLoRA SFT on 17K curated examples, then Gutenberg anti-slop DPO</dd>
      <dt>Hardware</dt><dd>One spot A100 · ~$40 of GPU, total</dd>
      <dt>Result</dt><dd>Lowest slop score of any 12B measured on EQ-Bench Creative Writing v3. Beats bigger models like Gemma 27B</dd>
      <dt>Reception</dt><dd>#1 trending on Hugging Face for a week after launch · 3K+ downloads</dd>
      <dt>License</dt><dd>Apache-2.0, weights + full recipe public</dd>
      <dt>Hosted</dt><dd>On <a href="https://featherless.ai/models/arbazsiddiqui/Ozan-v1-12B" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Featherless</a>, runnable from the Hugging Face page or over the API</dd>
    </dl>

    <Image
      src={banner}
      alt="Ozan the storyteller, a bard with an oud: the model's namesake artwork"
      widths={[640, 1024, 1440]}
      sizes="(max-width: 44rem) 100vw, 44rem"
      loading="lazy"
      class="banner"
    />

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The problem</h2>
      <p>
        Instruct models tell decent stories in a voice you can smell from
        across the room: “barely above a whisper,” “a testament to,” the
        reflexive “not just X, but Y.” The community calls it slop, and it
        comes from training on synthetic data that already contained it. The
        base model scores 9.47 on EQ-Bench's slop metric. Ozan scores
        <strong>5.30</strong>, a 44% cut, with the cleanest repetition score
        in the whole comparison field and zero degenerate outputs across 96
        test generations.
      </p>

      <Image src={chart} alt="Slop scores across models: Ozan-v1-12B scores 5.30, lower than every other 12B tested and lower than gemma-3-27b" widths={[640, 960, 1280]} sizes="(max-width: 44rem) 100vw, 44rem" />

      <h2>How it was made</h2>
      <p>
        Everything is public and reproducible. Six open datasets were reduced
        from 305K records to 17K by semantic dedup, a slop-density filter,
        and 13-gram decontamination against the benchmark prompts. Supervised
        fine-tuning ran as 4-bit QLoRA with completion-only loss, stopped
        early when the slop metric plateaued. Then a preference pass, DPO
        toward real public-domain book prose over AI prose. Merged, quantized to
        imatrix GGUFs, shipped.
      </p>

      <h2>Received</h2>
      <p>
        It launched to the #1 trending spot on Hugging Face and held it
        there for a week.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        “A genuine improvement on both slop reduction &amp; writing quality.”
        — Sam Paech, author of EQ-Bench, the benchmark it was measured on
      </blockquote>

      <h2>Try it</h2>
      <p>
        No download needed. Ozan is hosted on
        <a href="https://featherless.ai/models/arbazsiddiqui/Ozan-v1-12B" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Featherless</a>,
        so it runs right on the Hugging Face page or through the Featherless API.
        To run it locally instead:
      </p>
      <pre><code>ollama run hf.co/arbazsiddiqui/Ozan-v1-12B-GGUF:Q4_K_M</code></pre>
      <p>
        Weights: <a href="https://huggingface.co/arbazsiddiqui/Ozan-v1-12B" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ozan-v1-12B</a> ·
        quants: <a href="https://huggingface.co/arbazsiddiqui/Ozan-v1-12B-GGUF" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GGUF</a> ·
        recipe &amp; code: <a href="https://github.com/arbazsiddiqui/Ozan" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/arbazsiddiqui/Ozan</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-title { margin-block: 0.35rem 0.8rem; }
  .lede { margin-bottom: 1.6rem; }
    .banner { border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 2.2rem; }
</style>
